== install/toggle-default(true) ==

rbgs (0.9.0-d88b3186) installed in namespace "rbgs-system".

Check the controller:
  kubectl -n rbgs-system get deploy rbgs-controller-manager
  kubectl -n rbgs-system get pods -l control-plane=rbgs-controller
NOTE: compatibility for existing deprecated workload types is ENABLED
(controller.deprecatedWorkloadTypes.enabled=true).
Existing roles keep their own deprecated workload type and continue to reconcile,
while new uses — including switching between deprecated types — are rejected.
v1alpha1 writes return a deprecation warning.
For a new installation, prefer controller.deprecatedWorkloadTypes.enabled=false.

NOTE: chart v0.8.0 introduced a BREAKING CHANGE: values were regrouped under
`global`, `controller`, and `crdUpgrade`. Old top-level keys (e.g. `image.*`,
`replicaCount`, `schedulerName`, `portAllocator.*`) are SILENTLY IGNORED by Helm.
See the migration table in the chart README.md.

== install/toggle-false ==

rbgs (0.9.0-d88b3186) installed in namespace "rbgs-system".

Check the controller:
  kubectl -n rbgs-system get deploy rbgs-controller-manager
  kubectl -n rbgs-system get pods -l control-plane=rbgs-controller
NOTE: the deprecated workload types are DISABLED
(controller.deprecatedWorkloadTypes.enabled=false).
Only RoleInstanceSet is accepted; no RBAC or watches exist for Deployment,
StatefulSet, or LeaderWorkerSet. If this cluster was upgraded and still has roles
on those types, set controller.deprecatedWorkloadTypes.enabled=true, migrate
them, then switch back.
WARNING: the v1alpha1 schema defaults spec.roles[].workload to apps/v1 StatefulSet,
so a new v1alpha1 object is rejected even if it never sets `workload`. To keep using
v1alpha1, every role must set workload.apiVersion=workloads.x-k8s.io/v1alpha2 and
workload.kind=RoleInstanceSet; submitting the object as v1alpha2 does this by default.

NOTE: chart v0.8.0 introduced a BREAKING CHANGE: values were regrouped under
`global`, `controller`, and `crdUpgrade`. Old top-level keys (e.g. `image.*`,
`replicaCount`, `schedulerName`, `portAllocator.*`) are SILENTLY IGNORED by Helm.
See the migration table in the chart README.md.

== upgrade/toggle-default(true) ==

rbgs upgraded to 0.9.0-d88b3186 in namespace "rbgs-system".

Verify your effective values after upgrading:
  helm -n rbgs-system get values rbgs

Check the controller:
  kubectl -n rbgs-system get deploy rbgs-controller-manager
  kubectl -n rbgs-system get pods -l control-plane=rbgs-controller
NOTE: compatibility for existing deprecated workload types is ENABLED
(controller.deprecatedWorkloadTypes.enabled=true).
Existing roles keep their own deprecated workload type and continue to reconcile,
while new uses — including switching between deprecated types — are rejected.
v1alpha1 writes return a deprecation warning.
Take the deprecated-role inventory (see the chart README) and switch to
controller.deprecatedWorkloadTypes.enabled=false once it is empty.

NOTE: chart v0.8.0 introduced a BREAKING CHANGE: values were regrouped under
`global`, `controller`, and `crdUpgrade`. Old top-level keys (e.g. `image.*`,
